<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" ?>
<!-- Part 14 e2e scenario: combines two axes neither existing scenario
     exercises together: a genuine THREE-LEVEL type hierarchy
     (GrandparentType -> ParentType -> ChildType, vs. every other scenario's
     two-level BaseType/SubType) and the "retype-by-addition" local-
     extension pattern (test_vt_nested.NodeSet2's Drive/Motor never locally
     extend their nominal type), applied at the DEEPEST level only.

     UnitType: Optional "Value" : PropertyType/Double.
     GrandparentType: Mandatory "Unit" : UnitType.
     ParentType <: GrandparentType, declares nothing of its own: "Unit" is
       purely inherited, expected to produce zero new Virtual Types and no
       restriction of its own (ParentType just rdfs:subClassOf
       GrandparentType, structurally identical to it).
     ChildType <: ParentType, redeclares its OWN "Unit" instance still typed
       UnitType, but this specific instance node has a LOCAL child of its
       own, "Calibrated" : PropertyType/Boolean (Optional), that UnitType
       itself does not declare, so own_local_children is true and a Virtual
       Type IS minted here even though the TypeDefinition didn't change.

     Expect VT(ChildType, "Unit") to merge UnitType's own effective tree
     ("Value") with ChildType's local addition ("Calibrated"), i.e. recurse
     two dimensions deep from the third level of a type-inheritance chain:
     confirms get_cdt's recursive merge is correct across combined type-
     hierarchy depth and containment depth, not just one or the other. No
     contradiction expected. -->
